      "content": "Problem Description"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Write a program to solve Einstein's famous equation:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "E = mc2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "where,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "E = energy (in Joules)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "m = mass (in grams)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "c = speed of light (in meters/second2)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The speed of light is given by:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "c = 2.988 x 108 m/s2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Step 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "Use #define to set the value of the speed of light macro C to 2.988e8.",
        "Create a function-like macro calculate_energy() that takes an argument m and returns the value m * C * C."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Step 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "In main(), get user input for the double variable mass.",
        "Call the calculate_energy() macro by passing mass as its parameter.",
        "Store the return value in the energy variable.",
        "Print energy."
      ]
    },
